WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.400 --> 00:00:03.234
-Our first guests tonight
are the father/son duo

00:00:03.234 --> 00:00:05.300
you know from shows
like "9-1-1: Lone Star,"

00:00:05.300 --> 00:00:06.567
"The Grinder"
and "The Lowe Files."

00:00:06.567 --> 00:00:09.133
They co-created
and star in "Unstable,"

00:00:09.133 --> 00:00:10.601
which is streaming now
on Netflix.

00:00:10.601 --> 00:00:12.667
Let's take a look.
-Let's talk about us.

00:00:12.667 --> 00:00:14.334
-Us?
-I'm worried about us.

00:00:14.334 --> 00:00:16.367
-Are we an "us"? I've never
thought of us as an "us."

00:00:16.367 --> 00:00:18.400
-Exactly. Since you've been
here, you've made friends.

00:00:18.400 --> 00:00:21.367
That's great. But we haven't
spent much time together.

00:00:21.367 --> 00:00:23.033
-Mm-hmm.
Because at work, you're my boss.

00:00:23.033 --> 00:00:24.133
And at home, you're my dad.

00:00:24.133 --> 00:00:25.968
And everybody else is just
a normal friend.

00:00:25.968 --> 00:00:30.234
-Yes. So let's go somewhere
where we're not father/son

00:00:30.234 --> 00:00:32.968
or boss/employee.
Just friends.

00:00:32.968 --> 00:00:34.934
-Oh, my God. Are you going to
make me jump out of an airplane

00:00:34.934 --> 00:00:36.167
strapped face-to-face with you
again?

00:00:36.167 --> 00:00:37.701
Because that was terrible.
-Well, I loved it.

00:00:37.701 --> 00:00:39.300
And I'm the one
who got vomited on.

00:00:39.300 --> 00:00:43.234
-Please welcome to the show Rob
and John Owen Lowe, everyone.

00:00:43.234 --> 00:00:45.000
♪♪
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:45.000 --> 00:00:51.834
♪♪

00:00:51.834 --> 00:00:58.667
♪♪

00:00:58.667 --> 00:01:05.567
♪♪

00:01:05.567 --> 00:01:08.734
Welcome to the show, gentlemen.
This is very exciting for me.

00:01:08.734 --> 00:01:10.701
-It's very exciting for me
to sit

00:01:10.701 --> 00:01:13.234
in the least important position
in the studio.

00:01:13.234 --> 00:01:14.834
-There you go.
-I knew he was going

00:01:14.834 --> 00:01:16.067
to say something about this.
-Yeah, he was going to

00:01:16.067 --> 00:01:17.801
jump right in.
And I noticed he pointed there.

00:01:17.801 --> 00:01:19.767
He wanted you to sit there
and then he was going

00:01:19.767 --> 00:01:21.534
to be like, "Woe is me."
-Well, he wanted it

00:01:21.534 --> 00:01:23.133
to make it seem like it was
his decision.

00:01:23.133 --> 00:01:24.367
-That's exactly right.

00:01:24.367 --> 00:01:25.601
-You were going to sit here
no matter what?

00:01:25.601 --> 00:01:27.834
-That's what I want
everyone else to know.

00:01:27.834 --> 00:01:30.067
But yes.
-So you are --

00:01:30.067 --> 00:01:32.501
You are playing father/son
in this show.

00:01:32.501 --> 00:01:34.267
You are not playing
this father/son.

00:01:34.267 --> 00:01:37.033
But it does seem to be
a heightened version

00:01:37.033 --> 00:01:38.901
of your reality.
Is that fair?

00:01:38.901 --> 00:01:42.300
-It is. I think that Rob
is dangerously close

00:01:42.300 --> 00:01:44.701
to as insane as his character
is on the show.

00:01:44.701 --> 00:01:46.534
-Uh-huh.
[ Laughter ]

00:01:46.534 --> 00:01:48.300
-But it's -- yeah, it's --

00:01:48.300 --> 00:01:50.400
I mean, you want
to defend yourself slightly?

00:01:50.400 --> 00:01:52.100
[ Laughter ]

00:01:52.100 --> 00:01:53.901
-Yes.

00:01:53.901 --> 00:01:58.067
What happened was John Owen
would troll me mercilessly.

00:01:58.067 --> 00:01:59.634
And I think the last time I was
on the show --

00:01:59.634 --> 00:02:03.200
-I was going to say we
dove deep into the fact

00:02:03.200 --> 00:02:04.834
that you got trolled hard
by John Owen.

00:02:04.834 --> 00:02:08.067
-And thank you then
for making this show happen

00:02:08.067 --> 00:02:10.667
because it caught on
and people kind of liked it.

00:02:10.667 --> 00:02:12.100
And we were like,
"Maybe there's a show there."

00:02:12.100 --> 00:02:13.634
And that's how we came up
with the idea.

00:02:13.634 --> 00:02:16.267
-And so this premise, again,
you are not Rob Lowe the actor,

00:02:16.267 --> 00:02:18.667
and you are not his son,
but you are --

00:02:18.667 --> 00:02:20.234
I mean, is it safe
to say -- and again,

00:02:20.234 --> 00:02:21.834
correct me
if I offend your father

00:02:21.834 --> 00:02:25.133
in any way -- an egomaniac?
Maybe a bit of an egomaniac?

00:02:25.133 --> 00:02:29.634
-Yeah. No, I mean, yes. A bit?
Yeah.

00:02:29.634 --> 00:02:34.667
I mean, and to be clear,
this is like not a bit.

00:02:34.667 --> 00:02:36.767
We leave here and get
in the car together

00:02:36.767 --> 00:02:39.167
and it's straight to the car
mirror and like,

00:02:39.167 --> 00:02:40.400
"how do I look" and...
-Gotcha.

00:02:40.400 --> 00:02:42.234
[ Laughter ]

00:02:42.234 --> 00:02:45.334
-This is authentic.
-Now, see, I would --

00:02:45.334 --> 00:02:47.934
And again, you're going to be
less a part of this.

00:02:47.934 --> 00:02:49.434
-Okay.
-Thank God.

00:02:49.434 --> 00:02:50.334
[ Laughter ]

00:02:50.334 --> 00:02:51.334
-Because I would have thought --

00:02:51.334 --> 00:02:52.834
And again, I've met your dad.

00:02:52.834 --> 00:02:55.734
Your dad is a very cool person
when you meet him in real life.

00:02:55.734 --> 00:02:57.334
And I would have thought
he was a very cool dad.

00:02:57.334 --> 00:02:58.868
But based
on your social media,

00:02:58.868 --> 00:03:01.234
I've been completely disabused
of that notion.

00:03:01.234 --> 00:03:02.934
-First of all,
I'm glad to hear that. Yeah.

00:03:02.934 --> 00:03:04.467
[ Laughter ]

00:03:04.467 --> 00:03:08.400
Look, he is cool. I will
begrudgingly admit that --

00:03:08.400 --> 00:03:11.334
Well, I don't know about cool,
but he's a good dad.

00:03:11.334 --> 00:03:13.467
-He's handsome.
-Yeah, well, yeah.

00:03:13.467 --> 00:03:15.868
[ Laughter ]
Sure.

00:03:15.868 --> 00:03:18.601
He's a good dad.
But he's -- You...

00:03:18.601 --> 00:03:19.501
-Yes.
-...are...

00:03:19.501 --> 00:03:21.501
-Yes.
-...fairly insane.

00:03:21.501 --> 00:03:22.968
[ Laughter ]

00:03:22.968 --> 00:03:27.167
And, you know, I like to say
a benevolent narcissist, right?

00:03:27.167 --> 00:03:28.868
So yes.

00:03:28.868 --> 00:03:31.267
-Benevolent.

00:03:31.267 --> 00:03:33.367
-Well, now, Rob,
I have to say again,

00:03:33.367 --> 00:03:34.901
I have a couple
of boys of my own.

00:03:34.901 --> 00:03:36.667
I can't even imagine
how wonderful it must be

00:03:36.667 --> 00:03:37.767
to be on set together.

00:03:37.767 --> 00:03:39.100
And especially,
I should note as well,

00:03:39.100 --> 00:03:42.267
this show has been incredibly
well received so far.

00:03:42.267 --> 00:03:44.200
Are you just so happy
and proud every day?

00:03:44.200 --> 00:03:46.601
-It's pretty -- It's really
special because, I mean,

00:03:46.601 --> 00:03:49.367
you're a generation
behind me with your kids,

00:03:49.367 --> 00:03:52.234
but they'll get to a point where
they don't need you anymore

00:03:52.234 --> 00:03:54.167
and they're off in their lives

00:03:54.167 --> 00:03:57.534
and you have to figure out ways
to spend time with them.

00:03:57.534 --> 00:04:00.534
-Yeah.
-And that's what we have done.

00:04:00.534 --> 00:04:03.067
-Yes.
-And you obviously must love

00:04:03.067 --> 00:04:04.667
your son John because, again,
like I said,

00:04:04.667 --> 00:04:07.334
he's been very hard on you.

00:04:07.334 --> 00:04:09.801
[ Laughter ]

00:04:09.801 --> 00:04:12.434
This is one where
you wrote, Rob,

00:04:12.434 --> 00:04:14.534
you wrote "Who wore it best?"

00:04:14.534 --> 00:04:16.534
-I thought it was funny.
See, I'm doing

00:04:16.534 --> 00:04:19.934
the Angelina Jolie leg.
-And first comment was John here

00:04:19.934 --> 00:04:22.267
"Why did you start using
Instagram freely again?

00:04:22.267 --> 00:04:24.067
Go back to the podcast posts."

00:04:24.067 --> 00:04:26.167
[ Laughter ]

00:04:26.167 --> 00:04:28.634
-That was a good one.
I'm proud of that one.

00:04:28.634 --> 00:04:31.400
-This is again, this is
all him commenting on you.

00:04:31.400 --> 00:04:33.100
So there are you on the boat.
And now again, Rob,

00:04:33.100 --> 00:04:34.334
you tried to be funny here.
"Unreal.

00:04:34.334 --> 00:04:36.334
This drug-smuggling boat
landed on our beach

00:04:36.334 --> 00:04:37.834
in the middle of the night.
Happy Labor Day."

00:04:37.834 --> 00:04:39.701
-True.
-John wrote,

00:04:39.701 --> 00:04:41.200
"We need to start
teaching our parents

00:04:41.200 --> 00:04:42.834
Internet literacy and decorum."

00:04:42.834 --> 00:04:45.701
[ Laughter ]

00:04:45.701 --> 00:04:47.734
-Can I just quickly
just say that that's real?

00:04:47.734 --> 00:04:50.534
That boat washed up
and it was like a crime scene

00:04:50.534 --> 00:04:52.367
and he thought
he was important enough

00:04:52.367 --> 00:04:53.934
that he could just go there

00:04:53.934 --> 00:04:58.434
and start touching things,
like a live crime scene,

00:04:58.434 --> 00:05:01.934
and then post about it
on Instagram.

00:05:01.934 --> 00:05:06.467
And so it's kind of a bit,
but it's also very real.

00:05:06.467 --> 00:05:09.767
-You're trying to like --
It's an intervention of a sort.

00:05:09.767 --> 00:05:11.501
-At a certain point
you'd think he'd notice,

00:05:11.501 --> 00:05:13.934
but I just get to keep going
because he hasn't noticed yet.

00:05:13.934 --> 00:05:16.234
-This is really the best one.
It's the Oscars.

00:05:16.234 --> 00:05:17.367
-Yeah.

00:05:17.367 --> 00:05:19.334
-You once famously
performed the Oscars.

00:05:19.334 --> 00:05:20.734
-Oh, yes. Oh, yes.
-Yeah.

00:05:20.734 --> 00:05:22.267
Maybe the kids
don't remember it.

00:05:22.267 --> 00:05:24.067
-Well, they will now!

00:05:24.067 --> 00:05:26.501
-So you did a song and dance
with Snow White.

00:05:26.501 --> 00:05:29.300
-Yes, I did.
-And this is the photo

00:05:29.300 --> 00:05:30.667
that John put up that says,

00:05:30.667 --> 00:05:33.400
"Congrats to all the Oscar
winners, and to the losers,

00:05:33.400 --> 00:05:35.334
you still never did this."

00:05:35.334 --> 00:05:38.267
[ Laughter ]

00:05:38.267 --> 00:05:42.501
-That -- I was. Yeah.
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:05:42.501 --> 00:05:44.167
That one was mean.

00:05:46.234 --> 00:05:48.434
That one maybe was too mean.
-No, I don't think --

00:05:48.434 --> 00:05:51.834
Look, I'm good. The meaner,
the better. I can take it.

00:05:51.834 --> 00:05:53.200
-You're a good sport.
-Thank you.

00:05:53.200 --> 00:05:55.667
-Now, the other thing, though,
is, Rob, is it accurate

00:05:55.667 --> 00:05:59.300
that John did not
grow up watching your films?

00:05:59.300 --> 00:06:00.501
-Ask him.

00:06:00.501 --> 00:06:01.834
-Did you watch any of
your dad's movies?

00:06:01.834 --> 00:06:03.133
Oh, no, no, no. Ask him about
your favorite

00:06:03.133 --> 00:06:04.234
"West Wing" moment.
-Okay.

00:06:04.234 --> 00:06:07.000
What's your favorite "West Wing"
moment?

00:06:07.000 --> 00:06:09.667
-I don't have one
'cause I've never seen it.

00:06:09.667 --> 00:06:11.467
-You never watched
"The West Wing"?

00:06:11.467 --> 00:06:12.934
-I will say this much.

00:06:12.934 --> 00:06:15.434
Aaron Sorkin and the rest of the
cast, incredibly talented.

00:06:15.434 --> 00:06:19.367
-Okay now.
-I'm sure they're great.

00:06:19.367 --> 00:06:22.934
I bet that show is phenomenal,
but I've never seen it.

00:06:22.934 --> 00:06:24.100
-He's actually not kidding.

00:06:24.100 --> 00:06:26.000
-Now, how does
that make you feel?

00:06:26.000 --> 00:06:28.234
-Sad and lonely.
-And lonely.

00:06:28.234 --> 00:06:29.534
You would feel
like that either way.

00:06:29.534 --> 00:06:31.234
-I guess so
you realize -- And again now,

00:06:31.234 --> 00:06:33.334
I don't want to turn this on you
because, you know,

00:06:33.334 --> 00:06:36.234
we've talked about your dad's
imperfections a great deal here.

00:06:36.234 --> 00:06:38.901
I got to say, John, the fact
that you will only watch

00:06:38.901 --> 00:06:41.100
one of your dad's shows
that you're in...

00:06:41.100 --> 00:06:43.334
-Thank you.
[ Laughter ]

00:06:43.334 --> 00:06:45.334
-You know, I got to be honest,
it's a real, like,

00:06:45.334 --> 00:06:47.701
son of Rob Lowe thing to do.
-Look.

00:06:47.701 --> 00:06:49.767
[ Laughter ]
That is totally fair.

00:06:49.767 --> 00:06:51.701
[ Cheers and applause ]
-Thank you.

00:06:51.701 --> 00:06:54.167
-That's valid. That's valid.

00:06:54.167 --> 00:06:55.367
I watched "Parks and Rec."

00:06:55.367 --> 00:06:57.501
I watched that
before he went on it and then...

00:06:57.501 --> 00:06:59.767
[ Laughter ]

00:06:59.767 --> 00:07:01.000
...continued to watch it.

00:07:01.000 --> 00:07:02.634
-Oh, that's nice.
-Yes.

00:07:02.634 --> 00:07:03.801
-What about on set?

00:07:03.801 --> 00:07:05.701
Because you you have
less of a background.

00:07:05.701 --> 00:07:08.200
I know you're a writer,
but on camera,

00:07:08.200 --> 00:07:11.734
this show was a bit of a --
it's a big deal.

00:07:11.734 --> 00:07:14.200
Was it helpful to have your dad
on set as your costar?

00:07:14.200 --> 00:07:15.701
-It was.

00:07:15.701 --> 00:07:18.067
But he...

00:07:18.067 --> 00:07:21.667
He's difficult at times.
I would say that...

00:07:21.667 --> 00:07:23.968
There was this one moment --
I'll share this one moment

00:07:23.968 --> 00:07:26.234
because it was sweet
but also disturbing,

00:07:26.234 --> 00:07:29.801
which was that
the first day of shooting,

00:07:29.801 --> 00:07:33.000
it's the first shot
and I'm a little nervous.

00:07:33.000 --> 00:07:37.100
I haven't been -- I hadn't had
that much responsibility on set.

00:07:37.100 --> 00:07:38.868
And so it's like
I got to get on my mark.

00:07:38.868 --> 00:07:40.968
We're about to roll.
And right before we roll,

00:07:40.968 --> 00:07:43.934
you started to ramble about
how the mark was wrong

00:07:43.934 --> 00:07:45.467
and how someone was going
to cross in front of me

00:07:45.467 --> 00:07:47.567
and my hair looked off

00:07:47.567 --> 00:07:49.300
and maybe my chin
wasn't chiseled enough

00:07:49.300 --> 00:07:50.667
and whatever it was.
[ Laughter ]

00:07:50.667 --> 00:07:52.267
And it got me to this place

00:07:52.267 --> 00:07:54.534
where I was very frustrated
and very anxious.

00:07:54.534 --> 00:07:57.400
And then they called action,
and it was what my character

00:07:57.400 --> 00:07:59.400
was supposed to be doing
in that moment.

00:07:59.400 --> 00:08:01.100
And I thought to myself
afterwards, I'm like,

00:08:01.100 --> 00:08:03.868
"Damn it, did he just, like,
Miyagi me or something?"

00:08:03.868 --> 00:08:05.234
[ Laughter ]

00:08:05.234 --> 00:08:09.200
But I don't want to give him
that much credit, so...

00:08:09.200 --> 00:08:11.834
-Very, very well played, Dad.

00:08:11.834 --> 00:08:15.067
Very impressive.
It's a wonderful show.

00:08:15.067 --> 00:08:17.467
And it is just so delightful
to see you guys here in person.

00:08:17.467 --> 00:08:18.501
Thanks so much
for making the time.

00:08:18.501 --> 00:08:20.234
-Thank you.
-Thank you for having us.

00:08:20.234 --> 00:08:23.234
-The Lowes, Rob and John Owen,
everybody.

00:08:23.234 --> 00:08:25.534
"Unstable" streaming now
on Netflix.

00:08:25.534 --> 00:08:27.300
We'll be right back with
Judd Winick.

